<!-- Three options -->
<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark" id="compare-plans">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">Three straightforward options</p>
            <h2>Start with the level of support you need</h2>
            <p>The subscription plans spread the build cost over 12 months and include ongoing management. The one-off option is paid as a project and handed over at launch.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <article class="offer-card reveal">
                <p class="eyebrow">Managed starter</p>
                <h3>Essentials</h3>
                <p class="offer-card__price">From £125 <span>/ month</span></p>
                <p>A professionally managed website for a small service business that does not need regular articles.</p>
                <ul class="check-list">
                    <li>Five core pages plus legal pages</li>
                    <li>Hosting, SSL, backups and security</li>
                    <li>Reasonable updates to existing pages</li>
                    <li>Direct support from me</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="offer-card__note">12-month minimum, then monthly rolling with 30 days’ notice</p>
                <a href="/services/essentials-website-subscription/" class="btn btn--secondary justify-center w-full">Explore Essentials</a>
            </article>

            <article class="offer-card offer-card--featured reveal reveal--delay-1">
                <div class="offer-card__flag">Best for ongoing visibility</div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Managed growth</p>
                <h3>Growth</h3>
                <p class="offer-card__price">From £199 <span>/ month</span></p>
                <p>Managed website support plus help publishing and optimising articles supplied by your business.</p>
                <ul class="check-list">
                    <li>Seven core pages plus articles section</li>
                    <li>Hosting, SSL, backups and security</li>
                    <li>Your articles formatted and SEO-reviewed</li>
                    <li>Monthly reporting and practical advice</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="offer-card__note">12-month minimum, then monthly rolling with 30 days’ notice</p>
                <a href="/services/growth-website-subscription/" class="btn btn--primary btn-shine justify-center w-full">Explore Growth</a>
            </article>

            <article class="offer-card reveal reveal--delay-2">
                <p class="eyebrow">Own it from launch</p>
                <h3>One-off build</h3>
                <p class="offer-card__price">From £1,250</p>
                <p>A complete website project for businesses that want to arrange hosting and future support separately.</p>
                <ul class="check-list">
                    <li>Five core pages plus legal pages</li>
                    <li>Project-specific source code and assets</li>
                    <li>Full ownership after final payment</li>
                    <li>Optional hosting and support</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="offer-card__note">Typically delivered in 4–6 weeks</p>
                <a href="/services/one-off-website-build/" class="btn btn--secondary justify-center w-full">Explore one-off builds</a>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Plain-English comparison -->
<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-primary dark:bg-bg-primary-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">The practical differences</p>
            <h2>Compare what happens during and after the build</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="comparison-wrap reveal">
            <table class="service-comparison">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">What to compare</th>
                        <th scope="col">Essentials</th>
                        <th scope="col">Growth</th>
                        <th scope="col">One-off</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Starting price</th><td>£125/month</td><td>£199/month</td><td>£1,250</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Minimum term</th><td>12 months</td><td>12 months</td><td>None</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Core pages</th><td>Five</td><td>Seven</td><td>Five</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Hosting and maintenance</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Existing-page updates</th><td>Included</td><td>Included</td><td>Quoted separately</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Article support</th><td>Not included</td><td>Formatting, publishing and SEO advice</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">Website ownership</th><td>After minimum term</td><td>After minimum term</td><td>After final payment</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <p class="comparison-note">Updates to existing pages are included on managed plans. New pages, substantial redesigns, new functionality and third-party costs are scoped and quoted separately.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Ownership reassurance -->
<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="ownership-panel reveal">
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">No lock-in after the minimum term</p>
                <h2>Your website can leave with you</h2>
                <p>After completing a subscription’s 12-month minimum term, the plan becomes monthly rolling. You can cancel with 30 days’ written notice.</p>
                <p>If you leave, I will provide a portable copy of the project-specific website source code, content and relevant assets. You can then arrange hosting elsewhere without rebuilding the site.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ownership-panel__aside">
                <h3>What is not transferred</h3>
                <ul class="check-list">
                    <li>Hosting accounts and security credentials</li>
                    <li>Reusable internal tools and deployment systems</li>
                    <li>Third-party licences or services you do not own</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Decision guide -->
<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-primary dark:bg-bg-primary-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">A quick way to decide</p>
            <h2>Which route sounds most like your business?</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <article class="decision-card reveal"><h3>Choose Essentials if…</h3><p>You want a dependable website and ongoing help, but do not plan to publish articles regularly.</p></article>
            <article class="decision-card reveal reveal--delay-1"><h3>Choose Growth if…</h3><p>You can supply useful articles and want help turning them into well-structured, search-friendly content.</p></article>
            <article class="decision-card reveal reveal--delay-2"><h3>Choose one-off if…</h3><p>You prefer a project fee and are comfortable arranging hosting, maintenance and future updates separately.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Process -->
<section class="section-padding-lg bg-bg-section dark:bg-bg-section-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">The same careful process</p>
            <h2>Whichever plan you choose, the build stays personal</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 process-list">
            <li class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Clarify the scope</h3><p>We discuss your customers, goals, pages and content before I recommend the most suitable route.</p></li>
            <li class="reveal reveal--delay-1"><span>02</span><h3>Design and build</h3><p>I structure and hand-build the site, with clear review points and no account-manager handoffs.</p></li>
            <li class="reveal reveal--delay-2"><span>03</span><h3>Launch with clarity</h3><p>You know what is included, what happens next and who owns what before the website goes live.</p></li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQs -->
<section class="section-padding bg-bg-primary dark:bg-bg-primary-dark">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p>
            <h2>The details people usually want clarified</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>What happens after the first 12 months?</h3><p>Your subscription becomes monthly rolling at the same service level. You can continue for as long as it remains useful or cancel with 30 days’ written notice.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>What does an included update cover?</h3><p>Reasonable changes to content and layouts on existing pages are included. New pages, major redesigns, new functionality and third-party costs are quoted separately.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Can I move a subscription website elsewhere?</h3><p>Yes, after the minimum term. I will provide the project-specific source code, content and relevant assets so another suitable host or developer can run it.</p></article>
            <article class="faq-card"><h3>Do you write Growth-plan articles?</h3><p>You provide the knowledge and initial content. I help with structure, formatting, publishing and practical on-page SEO advice.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

